 "notes": "Sparse map of San Dimitri Point, the western tip of Gozo below 80 m cliffs: the shallow reef plateau where the boat moors, the drop-off to about 20 m, the boulder slope to 30 m and the swim-through under boulders at 18 m between reef and cliff. Coastline from OpenStreetMap; the reef outline is approximate and the rest follows the St Andrew's Divers Cove (gozodive.com) description, so positions are approximate. Whale Cave and Tal-Barba Cave lie about 1.2 km further south near the Inland Sea and are not drawn. The map origin is the reef (36.0688, 14.1837); the site coordinates lie about 500 m offshore to the north-west.",
